            <ArticleTitle>The appendix as the cause of chronic lower abdominal pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>122-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The records of 63 patients who had appendectomy for chronic lower abdominal pain were reviewed. Histologically 92% of the removed appendices revealed abnormality, and 95% of these patients were completely cured. It is concluded that appendicopathy does exist and could be the cause of chronic lower abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
